{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-08-06T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In Fez, Morocco, the Royal Palace—known as Dar al-Makhzen—has stood as a seat of power since the 13th century, when Morocco's rulers established a fortified royal city around it. Behind its high walls lie gardens, courtyards, mosques and royal residences spread across a vast complex still used by the king today, making it both historic and fully active.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FezMorocco_ROW6564333571_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FezMorocco_ROW6564333571_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Decorated gate of the Royal Palace of Fez, Morocco","Copyright":"© cgst26/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260805_FezMorocco\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Royal+Palace+of+Fez&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260805_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260805_FezMorocco"},"Ssd":"20260805","Name":"FezMorocco","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6564333571","FullDateString":"Aug 5, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Owls are far more than the wide-eyed birds they appear to be. Found on every continent except Antarctica, they are known for forward-facing eyes, flat facial discs that channel sound and specialised hearing. Many species hunt in near silence thanks to soft-edged feathers. Their eyes remain fixed in their sockets, so they rely on remarkably flexible necks to scan their surroundings. From forests to deserts, owls inhabit a wide range of environments and play an important role in maintaining ecosystem balance.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AdorableOwlet_ROW6516155898_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AdorableOwlet_ROW6516155898_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Florida burrowing owlet, Cape Coral, Florida, United States","Copyright":"© mlorenzphotography/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260804_AdorableOwlet\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Burrowing+owl&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260804_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260804_AdorableOwlet"},"Ssd":"20260804","Name":"AdorableOwlet","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6516155898","FullDateString":"Aug 4, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Colourful luzzus—traditional Maltese fishing boats—fill the sheltered harbour of Marsaxlokk, a village on Malta's southeastern coast. Just a short drive from Valletta, the island's capital, it remains one of the country's main fishing hubs, where daily life follows the steady pace of the sea. Home to roughly 4,000 residents, the village is also widely known for its lively waterfront, especially its popular Sunday fish market, and for the steady return of boats carrying fresh catches each morning.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BoatsMalta_ROW6191359643_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BoatsMalta_ROW6191359643_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Colourful boats in Marsaxlokk Harbour, Malta","Copyright":"© Klubovy/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260803_BoatsMalta\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Marsaxlokk+Malta&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260803_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260803_BoatsMalta"},"Ssd":"20260803","Name":"BoatsMalta","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6191359643","FullDateString":"Aug 3, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Finland is famous for the northern lights, its high happiness rankings, saunas and thousands of lakes. Helsinki adds history, design and the Baltic Sea to that list. The story begins in 1550, when King Gustav I of Sweden founded a trading town that would become Finland's capital in 1812. Today, a walk through the city can take you from Senate Square and the white-domed Helsinki Cathedral to the sea fortress of Suomenlinna, a UNESCO World Heritage Site accessible by ferry.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.HelsinkiBlue_ROW0990097537_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.HelsinkiBlue_ROW0990097537_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Helsinki's shoreline during blue hour, Uusimaa, Finland","Copyright":"© Miemo Penttinen/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260802_HelsinkiBlue\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Helsinki&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260802_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260802_HelsinkiBlue"},"Ssd":"20260802","Name":"HelsinkiBlue","Market":"ROW","Hash":"0990097537","FullDateString":"Aug 2, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Most landscapes change over thousands of years. Volcanoes can reshape them in a matter of hours, and on Hawaii's Big Island, they continue to do just that. Recognising the scientific and natural importance of this ever-changing environment, Hawaii Volcanoes National Park was established in 1916. For more than a century, it has protected more than 1,430 square kilometres of volcanic terrain, native forests and rare wildlife.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.HawaiiLava_ROW7372744216_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.HawaiiLava_ROW7372744216_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"A series of lava flows spill into the ocean, Big Island, Hawaii, United States","Copyright":"© Ken McCurdy/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260801_HawaiiLava\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Hawaii+Volcanoes+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260801_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260801_HawaiiLava"},"Ssd":"20260801","Name":"HawaiiLava","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7372744216","FullDateString":"Aug 1, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Some railways retire. The Virginia Creeper Trail simply changed gears. Stretching 55 kilometres through southwest Virginia, this trail follows a former rail line once used to haul lumber and iron ore through the Appalachian Mountains. Its unusual name traces back to the steam locomotives that laboured up steep grades in the early 1900s.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VirginiaTrail_ROW8255476190_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VirginiaTrail_ROW8255476190_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Aerial view of the Virginia Creeper Trail, Damascus, Virginia, United States","Copyright":"© Eifel Kreutz/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260731_VirginiaTrail\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Virginia+Creeper+Trail+Damascus&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260731_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260731_VirginiaTrail"},"Ssd":"20260731","Name":"VirginiaTrail","Market":"ROW","Hash":"8255476190","FullDateString":"Jul 31, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Some landscapes are famous. Monument Valley is legendary. Straddling the Arizona–Utah border within the Navajo Nation, this desert wonder is shaped by towering sandstone buttes that rise as much as 305 metres above the valley floor. Known in Navajo as Tsé Bii' Ndzisgaii—'valley of the rocks'—the region blends dramatic geology with living culture.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.NavajoNation_ROW6898030800_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.NavajoNation_ROW6898030800_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Monument Valley, Navajo Nation, Arizona, United States","Copyright":"© Westend61/Adobe Stock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260730_NavajoNation\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Monument+Valley&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260730_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260730_NavajoNation"},"Ssd":"20260730","Name":"NavajoNation","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6898030800","FullDateString":"Jul 30, 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A line of elephants emerges from the morning haze, calves keeping pace beside older relatives as they head towards a marsh. In Amboseli National Park, scenes like this unfold every day, shaped by water hidden beneath the ground. Meltwater from Mount Kilimanjaro filters through volcanic rock before surfacing as springs that keep the park's wetlands alive, even when the surrounding plains are dry. These permanent water sources sustain elephants, buffaloes, hippos and many other animals, while acacia woodland and open grassland support predators such as lions and cheetahs.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ElephantDay_ROW7064675180_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ElephantDay_ROW7064675180_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"A group of elephants, Amboseli National Park, Kenya","Copyright":"© Ibrahim Suha Derbent/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260812_ElephantDay\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Amboseli+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260812_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260812_ElephantDay"},"Ssd":"20260812","Name":"ElephantDay","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7064675180","FullDateString":"Aug 12, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Ships, storms and changing technology have come and gone, but the light remains. On Washington's San Juan Island, Lime Kiln Lighthouse has overlooked Haro Strait since 1919. Perched on a rocky bluff, its white flash continues to guide vessels through one of the Pacific Northwest's most important inland waterways. The lighthouse stands within Lime Kiln Point State Park, widely regarded as one of the world's best places to watch wild orcas from shore, with whales sometimes passing remarkably close to the coast.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LimeKiln_ROW6859587054_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LimeKiln_ROW6859587054_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Lime Kiln Lighthouse on San Juan Island, Washington state, United States","Copyright":"© Edmund Lowe Photography/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260811_LimeKiln\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lime+Kiln+Lighthouse&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260811_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260811_LimeKiln"},"Ssd":"20260811","Name":"LimeKiln","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6859587054","FullDateString":"Aug 11, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The best route here isn't built with concrete. Instead, the tide reveals a rocky path leading from Whytecliff Park to Whyte Islet in West Vancouver, Canada. A few hours later, the sea quietly covers the crossing again, making timing part of the experience. This shoreline has drawn visitors for generations. The tide opens the path; wet rocks keep you humble. The reward is a sweeping view back towards the beach and the hillside homes of Gleneagles.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.WhyteCliffP_ROW6700227959_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.WhyteCliffP_ROW6700227959_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Whytecliff Park, West Vancouver, Canada","Copyright":"© Aolin Chen/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260810_WhyteCliffP\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Whytecliff+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260810_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260810_WhyteCliffP"},"Ssd":"20260810","Name":"WhyteCliffP","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6700227959","FullDateString":"Aug 10, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"At first glance, they look like giant wooden shells rising above the trees. Look a little closer and every curve has a purpose. The Jean-Marie Tjibaou Cultural Centre, which opened in 1998, celebrates the Kanak people, the Indigenous inhabitants of New Caledonia, whose traditions, languages and customs have shaped the archipelago for thousands of years. Italian architect Renzo Piano designed the complex after studying traditional Kanak building techniques, reinterpreting them with laminated timber ribs, steel frames and modern engineering. Rather than copying historic structures, he created a contemporary design inspired by traditional Kanak grandes cases, or ceremonial houses.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.JMTjibaou_ROW6533820010_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.JMTjibaou_ROW6533820010_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Jean-Marie Tjibaou Cultural Centre, New Caledonia","Copyright":"© Fabien Astre/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260809_JMTjibaou\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Jean+Marie+Tjibaou+Cultural+Centre&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260809_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260809_JMTjibaou"},"Ssd":"20260809","Name":"JMTjibaou","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6533820010","FullDateString":"Aug 9, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Nature has a knack for balancing the impossible. In New Mexico's Ah-Shi-Sle-Pah Wilderness, towering hoodoos perch hefty rock caps on slender stems. Wind, water and ice have spent roughly 75 million years sculpting these remote badlands into an open-air gallery that feels more alien than terrestrial.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ValleyDreams_ROW6376883591_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ValleyDreams_ROW6376883591_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Hoodoos in Ah Shi Sle Pah Wilderness in San Juan County, New Mexico, United States","Copyright":"© Westend61/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260808_ValleyDreams\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Ah+Shi+Sle+Pah+Wilderness&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260808_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260808_ValleyDreams"},"Ssd":"20260808","Name":"ValleyDreams","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6376883591","FullDateString":"Aug 8, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In Copenhagen, Nyhavn Canal is a burst of colour and history. In Denmark's capital, bright, gabled houses lean toward the water, their reflections rippling beside old wooden ships. Carved out in the 1670s under King Christian V, this 17th-century canal once served as a busy gateway where cargo vessels unloaded goods straight into the city's heart. Sailors crowded its taverns, and the harbour gained a rough reputation long before it became the postcard-perfect place seen today.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ColorfulCop_ROW6097405388_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ColorfulCop_ROW6097405388_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Colourful homes line Nyhavn Canal, Copenhagen, Denmark","Copyright":"© emicristea/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260807_ColorfulCop\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Nyhavn+Canal+Copenhagen&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260807_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260807_ColorfulCop"},"Ssd":"20260807","Name":"ColorfulCop","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6097405388","FullDateString":"Aug 7, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In the Masai Mara, Kenya, the ground seems to move. A vast surge of wildebeest—hoofed grazers built for endurance—travel in tightly packed herds, drawn by fresh grass and water replenished by seasonal rains.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MaraCrossing_ROW6582779125_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MaraCrossing_ROW6582779125_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Migrating wildebeest crossing Mara River in Masai Mara, Kenya","Copyright":"© Manoj Shah/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260806_MaraCrossing\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Wildebeest&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260806_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260806_MaraCrossing"},"Ssd":"20260806","Name":"MaraCrossing","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6582779125","FullDateString":"Aug 6, 2026"}],"LocStrings":{"LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD":"Image of the day","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD_LEARN_MORE":"Learn more","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_DONATE_NOW":"Donate now","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_FACT":"Quick fact:","LOC_HOMEPAGE_GALLERY_CARD_TITLE":"Recent Homepage images","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_GALLERY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"Homepage image for {0}","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_TITLE":"On this day in history","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"On this day in {0}, {1}","LOC_HOMEPAGE_SHARE_TOOLTIP":"Share today's Bing homepage","LOC_HOMEPAGE_WALLPAPERDOWNLOAD_TOOLTIP":"Download this image. Use of this image is restricted to wallpaper only.","LOC_MUSCARD_DOWNLOAD_LINK":"Download this image","LOC_HOMEPAGE_WALLPAPERNOTAVAILABLE":"This image is not available to download as wallpaper.","LOC_HOMEPAGE_INFO_TEXT":"Info","LOC_BING_WP_APP_LINK":"https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2127455","LOC_BING_WP_APP_LINK_TEXT":"Get the Bing Wallpaper app","LOC_BING_APP_TEXT":"Get Bing Wallpaper on your devices","LOC_BING_APP_LINK_PC":"https://bing.microsoftapp.net/bing/?adjust=nk9xri2_dzfz5n2","LOC_BING_APP_LINK_MOBILE":"https://app.adjust.com/d93ddtl_a75k0gg?deeplink=sapphire%3A%2F%2Fwallpaper","LOC_BING_APP_DOWNLOAD_TEXT":"Mobile App","LOC_BING_WP_APP_DOWNLOAD_TEXT":"Desktop App","LOC_BING_APP_TEXT_MOBILE":"Get daily photos with Bing App","LOC_BING_APP_DOWNLOAD_TEXT_MOBILE":"Get","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_TOB":"Trending on Bing","LOC_HOMEPAGE_BELOW_SEARCHBOX_TOB":"Trending on Bing","LOC_HOMEPAGE_BELOW_SEARCHBOX_TOB_NEXT":"Next","LOC_HOMEPAGE_BELOW_SEARCHBOX_TOB_Close":"Hide trending on Bing","LOC_HOMEPAGE_TOB_TAG_NEW":"New","LOC_HOMEPAGE_TOB_TAG_HOT":"Hot","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ANSWER_FINANCE_TITLE":"My watchlist","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ANSWER_FINANCE_INCREASE_ARIALAB